  "story": {
    "id": "kenji_locker_detour",
    "person_id": "kenji_mori",
    "title": "The stuck locker run",
    "summary": "Kenji is comfortable sharing the sidewalk until a failed delivery bot blocks his usual door — comfort stays high, patience does not.",
    "beats": [
      {
        "id": "setup",
        "text": "After work Kenji walks from the transit hub toward his building, weaving past two delivery bots without breaking stride. He has an app ping: package in the lobby locker, ETA two minutes ago.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "approach",
        "text": "The last block is easy. He nods at a robotaxi dropping someone off, steps around a cleaner bot, and already thinks about dinner.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "encounter",
        "text": "At the entrance a bot sits dead-center on the ramp, status light amber, no motion. Another pedestrian squeezes past; Kenji cannot with his rolling briefcase. There is no on-screen error — just a machine pretending to be a planter.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "reaction",
        "text": "He waits ten seconds, then circles through the garage ramp. Mild irritation — the system usually works — but no spike of fear. He photographs the stuck unit and files an in-app report while walking.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "outcome",
        "text": "Package retrieved. Kenji still prefers robots to missing deliveries; he just wants stuck units to pull aside or call for help before they become furniture. His comfort score barely moved; his trust in recovery behavior did.\n"
      }
    ],
